%% LSEG Variance — "Questions this approach answers" (companion to the waterfall SVG)
%% v0.1 · conceptual · for validation · Viridian-proposed, not LSEG-ratified
%% The horizontal variance bridge is a waterfall (kept as SVG). This is the editable question map.
flowchart TD
  FRAME["v0.1 · Conceptual · For validation · Viridian-proposed, not LSEG-ratified"]:::frame
  HUB["The variance bridge answers:<br/>(companion to the waterfall — kept as SVG)"]:::hub

  Q1["Why did the forecast move?"]:::q
  Q2["Did Commit actually commit?"]:::q
  Q3["Did the tail convert at the assumed rate?"]:::q
  Q4["Did new pipeline materialise as modelled?"]:::q
  Q5["Which deals slipped — absorbed vs incremental?"]:::q
  Q6["How much of the forecast is deal-based vs overlay?"]:::q

  M1["Horizontal bridge: takes (adds) minus puts (reductions),<br/>every bar drills to named deals"]:::mech
  M2["Swing flag / downside calibration<br/>(the only source of downside)"]:::mech
  M3["Early Stage overlay: materialised vs converted rate"]:::mech
  M4["New Deals overlay: creation rate (promised vs materialised)"]:::mech
  M5["Puts, itemised — absorbed within the number vs incremental loss"]:::mech
  M6["Layer split — percent deal-backed vs percent overlay assumption"]:::mech

  HUB --> Q1 --> M1
  HUB --> Q2 --> M2
  HUB --> Q3 --> M3
  HUB --> Q4 --> M4
  HUB --> Q5 --> M5
  HUB --> Q6 --> M6
  HUB -.- FRAME

  classDef hub fill:#1F3864,stroke:#132444,color:#ffffff
  classDef q fill:#FFF3D8,stroke:#C8922E,color:#5A3E0A
  classDef mech fill:#E4F0EE,stroke:#17786B,color:#0F5045
  classDef frame fill:#FFF7E6,stroke:#C8922E,color:#4A4423
